
== B. bijectivity by exhaustion
   (a bitmap of the outputs where it stays in cache, w <= 12; and for every w the left-inverse test: if
    inverse(perm(i)) == i for ALL i of a finite domain, perm is injective, hence a bijection)
CHECK w= 4 (2^8 inputs), 1 round(s): all outputs distinct                                  ok (256 of 256, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 4 (2^8 inputs), 2 round(s): all outputs distinct                                  ok (256 of 256, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 4 (2^8 inputs), 3 round(s): all outputs distinct                                  ok (256 of 256, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 4 (2^8 inputs), 4 round(s): all outputs distinct                                  ok (256 of 256, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 4 (2^8 inputs), 5 round(s): all outputs distinct                                  ok (256 of 256, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 4 (2^8 inputs), 6 round(s): all outputs distinct                                  ok (256 of 256, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 4 (2^8 inputs), 6 rounds: inverse(perm(i)) == i for EVERY i                       ok (0 failures, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 8 (2^16 inputs), 1 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (65536 of 65536, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 8 (2^16 inputs), 2 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (65536 of 65536, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 8 (2^16 inputs), 3 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (65536 of 65536, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 8 (2^16 inputs), 4 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (65536 of 65536, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 8 (2^16 inputs), 5 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (65536 of 65536, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 8 (2^16 inputs), 6 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (65536 of 65536, 0.0 s)
CHECK w= 8 (2^16 inputs), 6 rounds: inverse(perm(i)) == i for EVERY i                      ok (0 failures, 0.0 s)
CHECK w=12 (2^24 inputs), 1 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (16777216 of 16777216, 0.1 s)
CHECK w=12 (2^24 inputs), 2 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (16777216 of 16777216, 0.2 s)
CHECK w=12 (2^24 inputs), 3 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (16777216 of 16777216, 0.2 s)
CHECK w=12 (2^24 inputs), 4 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (16777216 of 16777216, 0.3 s)
CHECK w=12 (2^24 inputs), 5 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (16777216 of 16777216, 0.4 s)
CHECK w=12 (2^24 inputs), 6 round(s): all outputs distinct                                 ok (16777216 of 16777216, 0.4 s)
CHECK w=12 (2^24 inputs), 6 rounds: inverse(perm(i)) == i for EVERY i                      ok (0 failures, 0.5 s)
CHECK w=14 (2^28 inputs), 6 rounds: inverse(perm(i)) == i for EVERY i                      ok (0 failures, 8.5 s)
CHECK w=16 (2^32 inputs), 6 rounds: inverse(perm(i)) == i for EVERY i                      ok (0 failures, 140.8 s)
CHECK PLANT: a round that reads the wrong half is NOT a bijection at w=12 (collisions found) ok (2363750 distinct of 16777216)
CHECK PLANT: the same broken round fails inverse(perm(i)) == i at w=8                      ok (65533 failures of 65,536)

== Q. quality of perm(i), i = 0 .. 2^22 - 1, at 64 bits (w = 32); thresholds are z-scores
   rounds   bit balance    avalanche  top-12 hist  serial corr   verdict
   1            2048.00       141.42  47412534.63      2048.00   fail
   2               2.90       141.42         1.60         1.38   fail
   3               2.08         3.62         0.71         0.03   PASS
   4               1.92         3.79         1.07         0.45   PASS
   6               2.24         4.47         0.55         1.62   PASS
   8               2.99         3.93         0.37         1.05   PASS
   (bit balance: max over 64 bits of |ones - N/2| / sd; avalanche: max over 64 x 64 input-output bit pairs of
    |flips - M/2| / sd, M = 20,000; top-12 hist: |chi-square - df| / sd of 4,096 bins; serial: |r| sqrt(N-1))
CHECK one round FAILS the quality tests (the tests can fail)                               ok 
CHECK two rounds fail the avalanche test                                                   ok (z = 141.4)
CHECK four rounds pass every test                                                          ok (1.92 3.79 1.07 0.45)
CHECK six and eight rounds pass every test                                                 ok 

== C. cycle walking onto a range that is not a power of four
CHECK N = 3,000,000 inside the domain 4^11: every output is in [0, N)                      ok (0 outside)
CHECK N = 3,000,000: all N outputs distinct, a bijection of [0, N)                         ok (3000000 distinct)
CHECK the mean number of permutation calls an index is near 4^11 / N = 1.398               ok (1.3981)
CHECK PLANT: clamping out-of-range outputs instead of walking loses cases (not a bijection) ok (2146209 distinct of 3000000)

== A. coverage accounting: the first K indices give exactly K distinct cases; shards are disjoint
CHECK indices [0, 1): distinct cases                                                       ok (1)
CHECK indices [0, 100): distinct cases                                                     ok (100)
CHECK indices [0, 1000000): distinct cases                                                 ok (1000000)
CHECK indices [0, 8000000): distinct cases                                                 ok (8000000)
CHECK indices [0, 16777216): distinct cases                                                ok (16777216)
CHECK two device shards, index ranges [0, 1e6) and [1e6, 3e6): the case sets are disjoint  ok (0 shared of 1000000 + 2000000)
CHECK PLANT: shards [0, 1e6) and [9e5, 2e6) share exactly their 100,000 common indices     ok (100000 shared)

